WEBVTT

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.940
INTRIGUE

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:50.940
Oh, here it is!

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:55.820
This was Long's work.
Of course, the article is all lies.

00:01:56.070 --> 00:01:59.700
Yeah, I guess they always are.

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:04.950
Thanks to this, now the CEO is able
to work in Shanghai.

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:08.080
After old man Chen was killed,

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:12.210
his son took over Chen group.
And he'll do whatever the CEO says.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:17.340
Actually, today's target is the son's
illegitimate child.

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:21.680
The guy from the Chinese embassy
who we're meeting today?

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:23.260
Yes, that's right.

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:26.890
He's not openly a member of
the Chen family.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:29.020
But it's possible that in the future

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:32.610
his existence could cause problems for us.

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:37.900
Since the Chen grandson has gone crazy,
the CEO intends to make himself

00:02:38.110 --> 00:02:39.860
the heir to Chen Group.

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:41.870
However,

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:46.660
someone in the Chen family could use the
illegitimate son to launch a counterclaim.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:51.250
So we're going to crush him now
before that happens?

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:52.380
Yep.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:54.750
Try not to arouse any suspicion.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:56.710
Um...

00:02:57.130 --> 00:03:00.880
Is the reason you're telling me so much
about the Company's plans

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:04.970
because you want me to become an employee?

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:07.310
It's just...

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.980
I can't make a decision about that
until Mr. Hayashi comes back.

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:13.860
Yes, yes, I know.

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:16.360
Look, your scar has vanished.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.900
Wow, it's gone.

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:21.410
My trademark...

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:25.030
But you know, you'll be 20 soon, Satoru.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:29.410
Don't you think it's time you stopped
relying on Mr. Hayashi for everything?

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:32.920
I think you should try
to decide for yourself.

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:42.180
Hey, Tsukasa...

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:46.300
I look weird, don't I?

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.060
Not a bit, Hiroki.

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:50.930
C'mon, you're laughing at me!

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.690
-Screw this!
-Hey, don't take it off!

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:56.690
Mr. Katsuragi's on his way to pick you up.

00:03:57.610 --> 00:04:00.570
Please, Hiroki. You need to fit in today,

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:03.030
so you can't worry about how it looks.

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:05.450
Yeah, I know.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:09.910
I'm sorry to be making you do this.
I really am.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:11.290
But...

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:13.580
You only need to stick it out
for a little longer.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:16.080
It's okay.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:18.800
I'm not doing this because you asked me.

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:21.210
I'm doing it because I decided to.

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:24.930
So don't worry about me.
I'll do a good job!

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:28.310
It's Satoru you should be worried about.

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:32.560
His door gets stuck all the time,
you know.

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:35.100
Watch out for Satoru, Hiroki.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:39.150
Just because you're doing a job with him,

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.360
doesn't mean you need to tell him
about our back door trick.

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:47.240
Even though he's an image user,
he might not be on our side.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:50.160
You mustn't trust him.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:58.130
That damn Katsuragi... How many times
is he gonna push that thing!

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:01.380
You mustn't fight
with Mr. Katsuragi either!

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:07.010
What's this? You off to
your school prom, Hiroki?

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:09.890
-Shut it, Katsuragi!
-Hiroki!

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:11.970
He started it.

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:13.770
Mr. Katsuragi...

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:15.980
If you make Hiroki mad today,

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:18.150
I won't be there to hold him back.

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:21.020
I was just saying he should
wear something over it!

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:24.360
He'll look suspicious as hell,
a fish shop owner dressed like that!

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:26.280
I was just about to put a jacket on!

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:29.910
A car will be here to pick you up
in 30 minutes.

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:32.410
Is the CEO in Beijing?

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:37.250
Yes, he is waiting for you,
and has arranged a Peking duck banquet.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:39.460
Let's go, Hiroki!

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:43.550
See you later, Tsukasa!
Have a good rest!

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:49.140
I'm sure the CEO

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:52.560
will ask me how I managed to
come back from being crushed.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:54.850
He must be very curious about that.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:59.230
Long will have been sure to report it.

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:02.070
His face was a picture!

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:06.860
But they won't have even the faintest idea
what my pet did.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:11.700
They thought I'd been crushed,
but here I am as alive as ever!

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:16.080
They don't even have images.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:20.750
So they'll never work out how I did it.

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:25.010
And I'm not going to tell them either!
Because that's my secret trick.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:28.010
I need to keep it secret
because I'm going to use it

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:29.840
to crush Satoru!

00:06:30.010 --> 00:06:32.680
What fun it'll be lying
to that bald bastard!

00:06:33.050 --> 00:06:36.430
And Satoru is wide open to attack
at any time.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:40.980
All I have to do is enter his peak
just once.

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:44.360
Just warp right in there!

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:48.110
Long's face! He looked like a pigeon
that'd been shot by a pea-shooter!

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:54.620
Now it's time to bring Meiling into play,
time for Satoru to see her peak.

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:58.620
And when he does, what will he do?

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:01.880
He'll take the bait, of course!

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:06.460
He'll take poor Meiling
and let her into his own peak.

00:07:06.670 --> 00:07:09.880
But who's this sneaking in
at the same time? It's Tsukasa!

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:14.010
Then on the next job with Satoru,
I'll crush him and say it was an accident!

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:17.770
What a good boy, Satoru is!
A good little idiot!

00:07:17.930 --> 00:07:20.940
He won't be able to resist
taking care of Meiling.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:22.900
After all, her peak originally comes

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:25.900
from Mr. Hayashi's peak!

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:40.540
We've just arrived. Where are you?

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:44.500
Over there.

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:49.510
There's someone sitting behind Satoru.

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:52.260
You stay in the car!

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:58.180
Does Hiroki know what he's
supposed to do?

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:02.310
Yes, we went over it again
on the way here.

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:04.190
All right, Satoru,

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:06.190
you can go.

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:07.860
O...Okay.

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:10.820
Oh, one more thing.

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:13.450
Don't tell Hiroki what we talked about.

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:15.820
That's for your ears only.

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:18.450
Yes, I understand.

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:20.080
Bye, then.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:28.460
Just as a reminder, it's your job to take
them both back afterward, Katsuragi.

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:33.380
I can't leave here until
I've confirmed the hospital

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:35.390
that the target has been taken to.

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:38.180
If it's the one we expect,

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:42.310
then we have Company connections there
so we'll get the information quickly.

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:44.520
But if it happens to be somewhere else,

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:47.270
I'll need you to tie up a few loose ends.

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:53.360
But most likely, so long as
those boys crush the target properly,

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:56.910
this job will be done and dusted.

00:08:58.580 --> 00:08:59.740
Hey, Hiroki,

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:01.750
did you lose some weight?

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:04.750
I just look different because
I combed my hair back.

00:09:05.670 --> 00:09:09.250
No, that's not it. Tsukasa hasn't been
eating recently, so I haven't either.

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:12.920
There's something I want to
ask your advice on.

00:09:13.300 --> 00:09:14.760
Seriously? We're on a job...

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:19.680
I know, but the only time I get to see you
is when we're doing a job.

00:09:20.350 --> 00:09:22.270
There's something else...

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:26.190
You can't tell anyone else
that I asked your advice about this.

00:09:26.480 --> 00:09:28.400
I'm not supposed to tell anyone about it.

00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:33.280
Says who? Katsuragi?
Or that woman who was in the car?

00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:36.740
Yeah, the woman.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:40.830
She's asked me to become an employee.

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:42.660
An employee?!

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:45.410
Yeah, and I'm really conflicted.

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:47.500
What do you think I should do?

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:50.250
You mustn't trust him.

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:54.670
If you're not supposed to tell anyone,
why're you telling me?

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:56.470
I shouldn't, but...

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:59.430
Tsukasa's older than me, right?

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:02.470
So I thought maybe he'd been asked too.

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:03.890
To become an employee?!

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:05.680
Of course he's not been asked!

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:08.270
You sure?

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:11.190
He might have been told
to keep it quiet as well.

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:14.230
Don't talk crap.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:17.950
Even if he was told to keep it quiet,
he'd still tell me.

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:22.120
Am I sure? Would Tsukasa really tell me?

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:26.330
He didn't even say anything to me
when he knew he might get crushed.

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:32.130
If he used Chinese, he could easily talk
about it without me finding out.

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:34.880
No, he wouldn't do that!

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:38.840
He did eventually talk to me before.

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:42.600
He even told me things he didn't want
to talk about.

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:46.890
I was raised by the Company
for the organ trade.

00:10:47.430 --> 00:10:50.980
We've been together so long, and yet
I didn't know anything about him...

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:54.570
Um, Hiroki...

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:58.240
Go be a damn employee for the damn Company
if that's what you want!

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:01.740
Even if Tsukasa has been asked,
what difference does it make?

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:04.330
It's your life. Make up your own mind!

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:06.160
Yeah, you're right.

00:11:06.580 --> 00:11:09.540
I need to think for myself.

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:10.920
But...

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:14.130
thinking for yourself is hard, you know?

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:15.000
Hey.

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:17.010
This is the place, Satoru.

00:11:17.210 --> 00:11:19.590
This door better be unlocked
like it's supposed to be...

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:36.270
Too slow!

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:40.950
You've only got to change a few memories.
What's taking you so long?

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:42.070
I'm sorry.

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:44.160
It's because you're slow

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:47.370
that Hayashi found a new pet
to replace you.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:53.630
Now then. Next, crush that woman.

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:57.960
Don't forget, I'll be timing
how long it takes you.

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:05.720
The clumsy oaf is your part, Satoru.

00:12:06.180 --> 00:12:07.180
Huh? Why me?

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:10.980
Because your door breaking all the time is

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:12.690
the only reason I'm even here.

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:17.190
It only doesn't open sometimes
when going to a valley.

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:20.440
It's a peak today, so it'll open for sure.

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:23.490
Everyone's making too much of
a big deal of it.

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:25.740
Yeah, but that's still why I'm here.

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:27.910
Ambassador, what a pleasure to meet you.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.830
There's Katsuragi.

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:32.160
What're you waiting for, Satoru?

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:34.710
Katsuragi's giving the signal.

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:35.830
Dammit.

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:42.760
Hey!

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:44.220
I'm terribly sorry.

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:48.760
What've you spilled? Is it alcohol?

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:52.310
He's asking you what you spilled.
What is it?

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:53.600
It's water.

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:56.940
It's water, so how about getting them
to dry it off with a hairdryer?

00:12:57.110 --> 00:12:58.940
What's wrong, darling?

00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:00.360
I'm soaked, that's what!

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:03.070
If you could take a seat
over by the socket.

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:04.200
What?

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:07.700
He's asking you to sit by the socket
so that the cord will reach.

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:09.370
Wait, that woman...

00:13:09.660 --> 00:13:11.790
-Is she his wife?
-Did you bring my spare jacket?

00:13:11.950 --> 00:13:13.120
I don't think you need to change.

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:16.250
-We're gonna crush him in front of her...
-May I have a moment?

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:18.750
There's something I'd like to ask you.

00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:20.880
It will soon dry off.

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:23.720
What? You can speak Mandarin after all?

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:27.050
Wearing wet clothes is
uncomfortable, isn't it?

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:32.520
You should dry them off, shouldn't you?

00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:33.770
Yeah, I should...

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:36.190
We're thinking of holding an exhibition
of Chinese dresses.

00:13:36.350 --> 00:13:38.900
Would you consider lending us
your collection?

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:40.940
Oh, how flattering...

00:13:41.770 --> 00:13:42.440
Dammit!

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:44.900
Think of a pleasant memory,

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:47.240
and just relax.

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:50.450
Okay...

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:07.760
You're my real dad, aren't you?

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:17.350
You're my real dad, aren't you?

00:14:18.730 --> 00:14:20.310
Did your mom say that?

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:22.610
See? It opened fine.

00:14:22.770 --> 00:14:24.190
No, Mom said you weren't.

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:27.150
So why do you think I am?

00:14:28.110 --> 00:14:30.160
Because I can tell that mom's lying.

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:33.870
She said you're rich,

00:14:34.120 --> 00:14:37.460
and she hates rich people
because they're all "black cats".

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:40.380
Do you hate "black cats" too?

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:42.420
Don't you know?

00:14:43.170 --> 00:14:45.380
It doesn't matter if a cat
is black or white.

00:14:45.590 --> 00:14:48.170
If it catches mice, it's a good cat!

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:52.970
You cheeky little scamp.
Who do you take after, I wonder?

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:03.860
You are my son.

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:12.320
This is it. If we make Chen say
"you're not my son" instead,

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:13.990
we can crush the ambassador easily.

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:16.450
And you're fine with that, are you?

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:19.830
His wife is right in front of him,
you know.

00:15:20.210 --> 00:15:22.170
What are you talking about, Hiroki?

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:24.920
-This is work.
-So what if it's work?

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:27.210
Does that mean anything goes?

00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:29.090
Don't you see how messed up this is?

00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:33.640
How's his wife gonna feel when her husband
gets crushed in front of her?

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:37.350
We couldn't do the job if we thought
about that kind of stuff.

00:15:37.890 --> 00:15:40.180
If his wife wasn't here,
would it be okay then?

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:44.150
What're we doing
any of this for anyway?

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:46.150
It's not for fun, is it?!

00:15:46.570 --> 00:15:49.320
Are you some kind of
crusader for justice now?

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:52.780
If you are, then what the hell
are you doing here?

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:55.280
I can't let myself think about it,

00:15:55.700 --> 00:15:59.370
'cause if I do, my thoughts all
lead to the same question.

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:02.370
Why hasn't Mr. Hayashi come back?

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:05.750
Being made to do jobs I don't wanna do...

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:08.170
Being asked if I wanna be an employee...

00:16:08.590 --> 00:16:10.840
If only Mr. Hayashi was here,

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:13.130
I could ask his advice about all of it.

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:15.640
But he never even calls me on the phone.

00:16:16.600 --> 00:16:18.600
Two years without any contact.

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:20.680
Was he lying to me?

00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:24.850
Was I an idiot for thinking I could live
with him forever?

00:16:26.810 --> 00:16:27.610
I can't...

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:30.280
I can't think about that.

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:32.950
Or else I won't be able
to shake the thought

00:16:33.150 --> 00:16:35.160
that he might have abandoned me.

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:37.240
'Cause he could have, right?

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:40.240
There's no law that says
he has to be with me.

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:43.540
And I'm old enough now

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:47.290
that I should probably just be happy
he shared his peak with me.

00:16:47.750 --> 00:16:48.840
And yet...

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:53.930
I still can't help wanting him
to come back.

00:16:54.470 --> 00:16:57.720
That's why I try not to think about things
and just do as Mr. Katsuragi says,

00:16:57.930 --> 00:16:59.970
like Mr. Hayashi told me to.

00:17:00.180 --> 00:17:03.600
'Cause if I don't think,
I can still believe he's coming back!

00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:06.690
-If you hate it so much, go back!
-What do I have to say?

00:17:09.020 --> 00:17:11.860
You played the clumsy oaf earlier.

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:13.690
So I'll do this part.

00:17:15.990 --> 00:17:18.030
What do I say in Chinese to crush him?

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:26.120
That's all I've gotta say, right?

00:17:26.790 --> 00:17:27.960
Okay, Satoru.

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:31.920
You head back and set up some guys
to take the fall for us.

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:33.800
Okay...

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:38.140
This guy's peak can be crushed

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:40.350
with just one short phrase.

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:44.270
Compared to that,
our peaks are much stronger.

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:46.190
But they're fake.

00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:47.650
I guess...

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:51.230
that's why we each long to be with

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:55.900
the real person who shared
their peak with us.

00:17:57.660 --> 00:17:59.910
Don't think about that stuff, idiot.

00:18:02.450 --> 00:18:03.660
No.

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:06.410
You are not my son.

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:14.170
You are not my son.

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:24.770
Darling?

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:28.060
Darling! What's wrong?

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:31.440
-What happened?
-Looks like a heart attack.

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:33.070
What's going on?

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:34.690
Here, a hairdryer.

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:39.070
You use it to dry things, right?

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:41.950
You were drying the ambassador's clothes,

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:44.160
and he suddenly had a seizure.

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:48.160
I spilt some water
on the ambassador's jacket...

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:50.370
Yeah...

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:52.540
Darling? No!

00:18:53.090 --> 00:18:54.920
-You mustn't move him.
-Please, say something!

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:58.920
-It could be his brain.-What's that damn Hiroki doing?

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:01.390
Hey, you're in the way.

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:02.430
Dammit!

00:19:04.010 --> 00:19:04.970
Huh...?

00:19:06.180 --> 00:19:08.100
I feel dizzy...

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:12.020
Gotta get to... the parking lot...

00:19:12.810 --> 00:19:14.190
Katsuragi...

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:17.820
Hey, you okay?

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:22.030
Yeah, they're taking him away now.

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:24.580
Yamako General Hospital.

00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:26.620
Some kind of seizure, apparently.

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:28.790
All going according to plan.

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:30.210
Now all that's left...

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:35.130
That was...

00:19:35.670 --> 00:19:38.380
Katsuragi, what's going on?!

00:19:38.800 --> 00:19:40.970
Hiroki just got put into an ambulance!

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:44.640
Huh? I've been looking all over for him.

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:48.600
Well, you weren't looking hard enough!
Hurry up and bring him back!

00:19:48.770 --> 00:19:52.190
Understood. I'll take Satoru and head over
to the hospital right...

00:19:52.350 --> 00:19:54.310
No! You can't!

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:56.440
You can't take Satoru.

00:19:56.650 --> 00:19:59.570
One of the floor staff got taken away too.

00:19:59.820 --> 00:20:03.030
Not one of ours. Must be one
from an agency.

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:05.410
Do you hear me, Katsuragi?

00:20:05.660 --> 00:20:09.540
Take Satoru back to Ikebukuro first,
then go to the hospital by yourself.

00:20:10.200 --> 00:20:14.830
I'll find someone who looks like Hiroki
and set them up as a fall guy.

00:20:15.330 --> 00:20:17.000
Then you switch them at the hospital.

00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:20.550
The ambassador's wife will be there,
so remember to cover your face.

00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:21.800
Do you understand?

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:26.800
It's okay. Just because he's in the same
hospital, doesn't mean he'll find out.

00:20:27.510 --> 00:20:31.350
They never even met, so even if Hiroki
does see something,

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:33.310
he won't know what it means.

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:38.730
What is it, Tsukasa?

00:20:39.020 --> 00:20:40.940
Let me find a pet of my own!

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:42.820
I'll show you I can raise one!

00:20:43.490 --> 00:20:46.820
Is that so? I'm impressed, Tsukasa.

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:50.870
Hayashi will be proud of you, too.

00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:56.580
What's this?

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:59.960
Louie Roeder Crystal Brut, one of...

00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:01.340
You must be new.

00:21:01.630 --> 00:21:03.090
Y...Yes.

00:21:03.880 --> 00:21:06.470
I prefer bottled water.

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:09.050
Make sure it's unopened.

00:21:13.180 --> 00:21:14.520
Hurry up then.

00:21:14.690 --> 00:21:15.810
Yes, sir!

00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:20.150
I know what the CEO's game is.

00:21:20.570 --> 00:21:24.860
He'll use the chance of seeing Mr. Hayashi
again as a carrot to keep Satoru working.

00:21:25.650 --> 00:21:26.910
It worked on me after all.

00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:31.080
I kept going for 12 years thinking I might
be able to see him again.

00:21:32.580 --> 00:21:36.870
Hayashi's imprints are all over Meiling.

00:21:37.210 --> 00:21:38.420
So if Satoru meets her,

00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:42.250
he'll never suspect that Hayashi
is already dead.

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:46.260
But it has to be me

00:21:46.470 --> 00:21:48.390
that brings them together,

00:21:49.260 --> 00:21:51.760
because that'll be my chance
to enter Satoru's peak.

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:54.930
I only need to enter it once

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:57.650
and I'll be able to crush him.

00:22:00.520 --> 00:22:02.690
Satoru is the lucky one, really.

00:22:03.230 --> 00:22:04.860
After all, if he gets crushed

00:22:05.030 --> 00:22:08.860
he won't have to keep waiting

00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:11.280
for someone who's never coming back.

00:23:50.130 --> 00:23:55.050
Artist: Katsuya Terada
